Write a minimal piece of code that reproduces the error, so one can
run it without needing lots of complicated data files etc.
Ideally use the reprex
package;https://community.rstudio.com/t/faq-whats-a-reproducible-example-reprex-and-how-do-i-create-one/5219

If you can only reproduce the problem with special data, then still
write a minimal R script that loads and runs _only_ the parts of the
code needed to reproduce the error (include all needed library calls
as well; the key is that whoever gets the file (and possible needed
data) should just need to run the script as-is, with no local
modification (_including_ file names; do not use any absolute paths,
and no complex relative paths; ideally everything should be in the
same folder).

Finn

