> this is hard to tell, as its not possible to rerun it here.
>
> I include a small example how this can be done. it can be annoying to
> get the linear predictor from the sample, but using
> 'inla.posterior.sample.eval', it is already predefined.
>
> you can read about this in the vignette:
>
>
