On Sun, 2023-06-25 at 07:35 -0700, You Zhou wrote:
> Hello: Havard
> It is my problem, i did not assign the number of threads and nodes on
> HPC, so it uses the default upper limit.

good. there is a limit how many threads that can be used. without
PARDISO, then its basically number of hyperparameters x 2. in the
integration phase it can use more. in the optimisation phase it can use
more, if you enable nested parallel, ie num.threads="8:2", f.ex.

this paper

Statistics and Computing
(2023) 33:25
https://doi.org/10.1007/s11222-022-10192-1
ORIGINAL PAPER
Parallelized integrated nested Laplace approximations for fas....

discuss this

